      "kind": "takeaways",
      "heading": "The short version",
      "html": "<ul><li>The Care Inspectorate regulates childminders in Scotland. Ofsted and CQC do not.</li><li>It uses the Health and Social Care Standards and a quality framework graded from 1 to 6.</li><li>Self-evaluation is ongoing. You judge the service and keep proof.</li><li>It finds gaps early. Acting on them is what helps.</li><li>Quickler keeps your walk and proof. It is not a children's records, register or child protection system.</li><li>A sole childminder starts with the 14-day free trial. Quickler is not linked to the Care Inspectorate.</li></ul>"
